From: Radeon24 <Radeon24@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] leds: trigger: netdev: stop the software blink before offloading

The trigger drives the LED in software until its mode can be offloaded:
a blink it started, or a brightness it queued, could still run after
the offload and overwrite the setting handed to the hardware (PHY LEDs
of the BCM54612E left lit without activity).
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Radeon24 <Radeon24@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/leds/trigger/ledtrig-netdev.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/leds/trigger/ledtrig-netdev.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/trigger/ledtrig-netdev.c
@@ -85,6 +85,14 @@ static void set_baseline_state(struct le
 
 	/* Already validated, hw control is possible with the requested mode */
 	if (trigger_data->hw_control) {
+		/*
+		 * The LED may have been driven in software just before, with a
+		 * blink still running or a brightness still queued: stop and
+		 * flush them, or they overwrite the setting handed to the
+		 * hardware.
+		 */
+		led_stop_software_blink(led_cdev);
+		flush_work(&led_cdev->set_brightness_work);
 		led_cdev->hw_control_set(led_cdev, trigger_data->mode);
 
 		return;
